└── README.md




Why start with the model?

Imagine a user submits:

{
    "title": "Database Connection Timeout",
    "description": "Users cannot access the portal after deployment.",
    "priority": "High"
}

How does FastAPI know:

title must be a string?
priority is required?
description cannot be missing?

It doesn't...

unless we define a Pydantic Model.


AI ORCHESTRATOR

What is the AI Orchestrator?

Imagine you're the manager of a hospital.

A patient comes in and says:

"I have chest pain."

Does the manager immediately treat the patient?

❌ No.

The manager decides:

Should I send them to Cardiology?
Neurology?
Emergency?
General Physician?

The manager doesn't solve the problem.

He decides who should solve it.

Our AI Orchestrator is exactly that manager.



Why I recommend it
It's built for RAG — MarkdownHeaderTextSplitter preserves the document hierarchy instead of splitting at arbitrary character counts.
Our documents already use Markdown headings consistently, so we're taking advantage of the structure we've created.
It scales. If tomorrow you add 500 more documents, the same loader works without changes.

It's interview-friendly. You can honestly say:

"I used LangChain's MarkdownHeaderTextSplitter so the retrieval system indexes logical sections like Symptoms, Root Cause, and Resolution instead of arbitrary chunks."

The final Knowledge Agent flow
